    "result_text": "The project has a single test class (the acceptance suite), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a derived `membershipTier` field returning `SILVER` when an owner is unique (`namesakeCount == 0`) and has an email, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nTwo small, well-placed edits following the existing `membershipNumber` pattern:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient` `getMembershipTier()` getter that derives the tier from the owner's own `namesakeCount` and `email` fields (single responsibility, right next to the analogous `getMembershipNumber()`).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipTier` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field, and MapStruct's name-based mapping wires `getMembershipTier()` into the JSON response automatically \u2014 no mapper changes or duplicated logic needed.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass and the full suite is green (2/2, BUILD SUCCESS).",
